.TH AURAPASS-NATIVE-HOST 1 "2026-10-21" "AuraPass 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aurapass-native-host \- Firefox native-messaging relay for AuraPass
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aurapass-native-host
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aurapass-native-host
is started by Firefox, not by the user. It speaks the browser's native-messaging
protocol on standard input and output and relays the already-encrypted frames
to the local AuraPass bridge. The extension never opens a loopback WebSocket in
Firefox, so HTTPS-Only Mode and Local Network Access restrictions do not affect
it.
.PP
The native-messaging manifest is installed at
.I /usr/lib/mozilla/native-messaging-hosts/aurapass_bridge.json
and only allows the signed extension id
.IR aurapass@aurapass.invalid .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AURAPASS_CONFIG_DIR
Overrides the directory that holds the bridge port and pairing token.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aurapass (1),
.BR aurapass-bridge (1),
.BR aurapass-desktop (1)
